# The store. The database is the record; a binary file in git is a record
# nobody can review, and records/ is the reviewable half.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Build output.
/mustur

# Claude Code's own directory, which is the machine's rather than the
# repository's: settings somebody set for themselves, and the worktrees agents
# work in. The worktrees are the sharp end — each is a checkout of this
# repository living inside it, so `git add -A` in the main checkout stages the
# whole tree twice ([MUS-F-0065](records/findings.md#mus-f-0065)).
/.claude/

# CI checks the StrucGu catalog out here for conformance (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
# It is never committed, and a records refresh branch fails the export-scope
# gate on any untracked file outside the export, so it is ignored.
/.strucgu/
